id: interface/yawn-capability-tags-v1
title: "YAWN capability tags v1"
kind: interface-contract
status: active
updated: 2026-08-10

purpose: >
  Make every public capability tag a usable instruction or a real path into the
  interface rather than decorative marketing copy.

initial_tags:
  - id: orient-this
    label: ORIENT THIS
    instruction: "Orient this source. Show where I am, what remains open, and one reversible next move."
  - id: show-what-changed
    label: SHOW WHAT CHANGED
    instruction: "Compare this with the last trusted pulse and show only material changes."
  - id: rank-next-moves
    label: RANK NEXT MOVES
    instruction: "Rank no more than three reversible movements and explain why the first outranks the others."
  - id: explain-why
    label: EXPLAIN WHY
    instruction: "Explain the source, assumptions, uncertainty, and ranking reason without rewriting the observation."
  - id: prepare-work-order
    label: PREPARE A WORK ORDER
    instruction: "Prepare a bounded draft work order. Do not authorize or execute it."

rules:
  - a tag copies its complete instruction
  - the copied state is announced to assistive technology
  - a tag may also open the relevant local composer or demonstration
  - 1.1A performs no live model call or API-key persistence

schema_version: yawn.capability_tags.v1
